␀␀␀Save game?    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Saved Successfully    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Hand the Nintendo DS over to␀␀␀Player 1. Touch the OK icon␀␀␀when Player 1 is ready.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Hand the Nintendo DS over to␀␀␀Player 2. Touch the OK icon␀␀␀when Player 2 is ready.    ␀␀␀	␀␀␀Saving...␀␀␀Do not touch the Game Card␀␀␀or the Power Button    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Restart mission?    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Surrender and quit?    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Continue previously saved␀␀␀mission?␀␀␀If you don't, all mission info␀␀␀will be overwritten.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀All your cards have been␀␀␀removed! You can't draw␀␀␀any more cards!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀Battle has reached␀␀␀48 Hour limit! It's a Draw!␀␀␀Neither player wins!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀"Ghosted" cards mean you␀␀␀have reached that card's␀␀␀inventory maximum!+␀␀␀    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀Welcome to Battles of Prince of Persia!␀␀␀␀)␀␀␀Since this is your first game, we'll take%␀␀␀some time to introduce you to some of'␀␀␀the game's basic controls and concepts.)␀␀␀Let's start with moving around the map to,␀␀␀see the kind of field you'll be fighting on.␀␀␀But first...'␀␀␀If ever you're not sure about how to do)␀␀␀something, you should check the Help text$␀␀␀in the lower half of the top screen.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Now... get ready to fight.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Viewing the Battle Map -␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀To move the map view, hold +Control Pad&␀␀␀Up then touch the bottom screen in the,␀␀␀direction you want to scroll. Give it a try!    	␀␀␀*␀␀␀Did you notice that the top screen changed&␀␀␀into a minimap when you were scrolling␀␀␀around?'␀␀␀Well, the top screen displays plenty of-␀␀␀game information during the battle, including-␀␀␀unit and terrain info, minimap and lots more!)␀␀␀Depending on what you're doing, different-␀␀␀information screens will be available to help␀␀␀you out.    ␀␀␀+␀␀␀If there's more than one information screen+␀␀␀use +Control Pad Left or +Control Pad Right"␀␀␀to cycle through them. Try it now.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀$␀␀␀- Displaying Unit and Terrain Info -␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀Sometimes you'll need to know something/␀␀␀specific about the unit or the terrain (such as␀␀␀how far a unit can go).(␀␀␀Units have two information types: Status␀␀␀(top screen) and Range (map).    ␀␀␀*␀␀␀Hold the L Button or R Button and touch an+␀␀␀empty terrain square (terrain info) or unit␀␀␀(unit info). Give it try!    	␀␀␀)␀␀␀There are other types of Range. While you*␀␀␀hold the L Button or R Button touch a unit-␀␀␀multiple times to see if it has other Ranges.+␀␀␀Also keep in mind that +Control Pad Left or,␀␀␀+Control Pad Right cycles through the unit's␀␀␀information screens.,␀␀␀Ok, time to apply what you've learnt so far.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Let's start playing!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Deploying Your Army -␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀At the start of each battle, your units start+␀␀␀placed in a default set-up. This allows you,␀␀␀to jump straight into the action by touching%␀␀␀the OK (checkmark) icon on the bottom(␀␀␀screen. Or, you can place your units how	␀␀␀you want.0␀␀␀To do this, just touch and slide (this is called,␀␀␀"dragging") a unit to the highlighted square'␀␀␀of your choice. These squares represent&␀␀␀your deployment zones. Note, you can't*␀␀␀place your units in enemy deployment zones␀␀␀(squares highlighted in red).)␀␀␀Choosing your army set-up is useful since#␀␀␀you can take advantage of your deck(␀␀␀selection through better unit placement.)␀␀␀Try placing some units now. Touch OK when␀␀␀you're done.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Selecting a Card -␀␀␀␀/␀␀␀Battles of Prince of Persia is driven by cards.,␀␀␀In other words, different cards allow you to#␀␀␀perform different kinds of actions.*␀␀␀Touch a card and look at the top screen to)␀␀␀view the card's info. So, what can you do␀␀␀after selecting a card?␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Playing a Card -␀␀␀␀,␀␀␀Dragging a card brings up your play options:␀␀␀PREVIEW EFFECT, PLAY EFFECT or␀␀␀GIVE ORDERS..␀␀␀For now, let's just concentrate on giving your␀␀␀units Orders.␀␀␀␀)␀␀␀You can give as many orders as the card's$␀␀␀Order Value (the number shown on the␀␀␀picture of the card) allows.(␀␀␀Go ahead, touch a card, drag it over the)␀␀␀Give Order box and "drop" it (to "drop" a+␀␀␀card, just take your stylus of the screen)!    ␀␀␀+␀␀␀Ok, you've selected a card that you can use"␀␀␀for PREVIEW EFFECT or PLAY EFFECT.␀␀␀␀&␀␀␀PREVIEW EFFECT allows you to see which$␀␀␀units can be affected by the effect.␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀Playing a card for Effects can change a'␀␀␀unit's stats, do direct damage, or give!␀␀␀multiple orders to the same unit.-␀␀␀To use the card, drag and drop it over either&␀␀␀the PREVIEW EFFECT or PLAY EFFECT box.␀␀␀Give a try it!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    	␀␀␀)␀␀␀The card you've played has been discarded+␀␀␀(this card is marked as Discard on the card␀␀␀info screen).+␀␀␀This means that the card will be reshuffled␀␀␀back into your deck later.␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀Effects that discard can be strong because*␀␀␀you'll have a chance to use them again and␀␀␀again during the battle.    	␀␀␀*␀␀␀The card you've played for Effect has been*␀␀␀removed from the game (this card is marked#␀␀␀as Remove on the card info screen).,␀␀␀This means that the card won't be reshuffled-␀␀␀back into your deck for the remainder of this␀␀␀battle.)␀␀␀Removed from the game cards are generally(␀␀␀strong but can only be used once. Try to,␀␀␀choose key moments to call on their effects.    ␀␀␀,␀␀␀Wait! You can't use this card to Give Orders*␀␀␀right now because you have no Ready units.␀␀␀␀+␀␀␀Cards are automatically "locked" if none of*␀␀␀your units can be selected for the desired␀␀␀action.    ␀␀␀/␀␀␀Wait! You can't use this card for Effects right)␀␀␀now because either you can't pay the Cost"␀␀␀or there are no Targets available.+␀␀␀Cards are automatically "locked" if none of*␀␀␀your units can be selected for the desired␀␀␀action.    ␀␀␀,␀␀␀If all your cards become "locked", just pass,␀␀␀your turn since you have no more valid units␀␀␀to use.    ␀␀␀*␀␀␀Note: To cycle quickly through your units,(␀␀␀simply press +Control Pad Down to select#␀␀␀the next Ready unit. Give it a try!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Passing Your Turn -␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀You can always pass your turn, even if you(␀␀␀haven't played a card. Sometimes waiting&␀␀␀can give you a key tactical advantage.%␀␀␀Simply touch the Turn (double-arrows),␀␀␀icon on the bottom screen to pass your turn.␀␀␀␀+␀␀␀Be careful! The hour ends when both players)␀␀␀pass one right after another so you might+␀␀␀end up doing nothing if you pass too often!    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Giving Orders -␀␀␀␀+␀␀␀When you select a unit to give it Orders, a*␀␀␀number of squares will become highlighted.)␀␀␀These squares show where the unit can go.)␀␀␀How far the unit goes depends on its Move(␀␀␀stat and the kind of terrain it crosses.&␀␀␀Card effects can also affect movement.-␀␀␀To move a unit, drag the unit to or touch the,␀␀␀destination square. Touch the Stay (hand) or-␀␀␀Move (footprint) icons to complete the order.*␀␀␀To cancel a selection or incomplete order,*␀␀␀just touch the Back (X) icon. At any time,%␀␀␀touch the Turn icon to end your turn.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    ␀␀␀␀␀␀1    ␀␀␀0␀␀␀Unit facing is crucial part of Battles of Prince*␀␀␀of Persia as it affects which units it can(␀␀␀attack and how well the unit can defend.    ␀␀␀,␀␀␀A selected unit's current facing is shown by,␀␀␀the moving triangle. To change facing, touch)␀␀␀Facing (white arrow) icon. Give it a try!    	␀␀␀.␀␀␀If a unit can attack multiple enemies in Melee+␀␀␀combat, change the facing to switch to your␀␀␀desired target..␀␀␀In Missile combat, facing dictates which units'␀␀␀you can and can't attack since a unit's'␀␀␀firing arc is determined by its facing.+␀␀␀Attacks from the side or the back gives the(␀␀␀attacker the upper hand so avoid leaving,␀␀␀your side or back open with a facing change.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Attacking -␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀Red squares are enemy Zones of Control.+␀␀␀Entering one means you must stop and fight,+␀␀␀so you should do it only when you're ready.,␀␀␀Before you confirm the move, look at the top-␀␀␀screen to check out the Battle Preview to get,␀␀␀a rundown of the combat different modifiers.+␀␀␀The prediction at the bottom of the preview0␀␀␀screen tells you how the battle is likely to go..␀␀␀While not always accurate, it is a good guide.*␀␀␀Once you're happy with a possible outcome,*␀␀␀simply tap the Fight (crossed-swords) icon␀␀␀to watch the results.+␀␀␀Note that a unit cannot go from one enemy's*␀␀␀Zone of Control to another one in the same␀␀␀turn.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Shooting -␀␀␀␀.␀␀␀Units with a Missile Stat can fire at an enemy,␀␀␀that is in the missile unit's firing arc and␀␀␀MaxRange stat.+␀␀␀To check a missile unit's range, hold the L%␀␀␀Button or R Button and touch the unit␀␀␀until Missile Range appears./␀␀␀Also, since it is a ranged attack, the attacker'␀␀␀never receives any damage regardless of␀␀␀the combat result.-␀␀␀Take note! A unit can't shoot if it has moved'␀␀␀in the same turn (facing change doesn't+␀␀␀count as moved) or if it's in an enemy ZoC.    ␀␀␀'␀␀␀When a unit has completed an order, its*␀␀␀Status is changed to Used and the unit can+␀␀␀no longer receive further orders this hour.'␀␀␀Once Used, the unit icon becomes greyed'␀␀␀out. All Used units become Ready at the␀␀␀beginning of the next hour.*␀␀␀You can also check a unit's current Status#␀␀␀by calling up its Unit Info screen.    ␀␀␀(␀␀␀Units become Stunned when they lose more␀␀␀than 18 HPs in one one attack.␀␀␀␀&␀␀␀A unit that is Stunned becomes Used at␀␀␀the beginning of the next hour.    ␀␀␀"␀␀␀Units become Broken when they lose-␀␀␀more than half their current HP in one attack&␀␀␀AND fail the accompanying morale test.'␀␀␀Broken units withdraw at 1/2 Move speed␀␀␀towards the closest map edge.␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀Passing the morale test means the unit has-␀␀␀the courage to stay but is disorganized. As a␀␀␀result, the unit becomes Used.-␀␀␀Every hour, Broken units get a Rally (Morale)&␀␀␀test. Success (automatic if in Command#␀␀␀Range) means the unit becomes Used.,␀␀␀Broken units that fail continue to withdraw.(␀␀␀Withdrawing units that reach the edge of␀␀␀the map are removed from play.    ␀␀␀,␀␀␀Push Backs occur when a unit loses 9 or more(␀␀␀HPs in one attack. The unit is moved one*␀␀␀square directly away from the attacker and&␀␀␀attackers move  into the square of the&␀␀␀defender. Units Stunned in combat also␀␀␀suffer a Push Back.    ␀␀␀'␀␀␀Units that cannot move away from a Push*␀␀␀Back (blocking unit or prohibited terrain)␀␀␀suffer 50% more damage!.␀␀␀A good tactic is to move your units to cut-off*␀␀␀enemy retreats or attack enemy groups that␀␀␀block themselves.    ␀␀␀,␀␀␀When a General is lost several things occur:,␀␀␀first, all friendly units become temporarily)␀␀␀demoralized and lose their will to fight;+␀␀␀second, the player can no longer play cards+␀␀␀for Effects and must rely on Give Orders to␀␀␀carry the day;&␀␀␀third, the maximum number of cards the(␀␀␀player can have at the beginning of each
␀␀␀hour is 4.)␀␀␀So try to make sure your General is never␀␀␀left alone to fend for himself.    	␀␀␀+␀␀␀Stats Down means that the affected unit has*␀␀␀lost enough HPs to lose combat efficiency.␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀Check "Stats Down In" on the the unit info*␀␀␀screen to see how many HPs are left before␀␀␀a unit suffers efficiency loss.)␀␀␀Some units go berserk after a Stats Down.$␀␀␀These units actually get stronger as␀␀␀they lose HPs.    ␀␀␀%␀␀␀Each unit stat (Move, Melee, Missile,)␀␀␀etc.) has a maximum. When reached, excess&␀␀␀stat increases have no further effect.    	␀␀␀+␀␀␀Victory Points (or VP) are key to winning a(␀␀␀battle but VP conditions can change each-␀␀␀battle so check the VP info screen regularly.-␀␀␀If two players get VPs at the same time, then,␀␀␀the player whose turn it is gets them first.-␀␀␀The battle is over as soon as one player gets&␀␀␀the required amount of VPs for the win'␀␀␀condition, or when a player has no more"␀␀␀units left on the field of battle.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Starting a New Hour -␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀At the beginning of each new hour: VPs are-␀␀␀given out for holding objectives, Rally tests+␀␀␀are made for any Broken units, card Effects(␀␀␀and unit Status are updated, and players,␀␀␀can draw new cards to replenish their hands.    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- Discard -␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀At the beginning of each new hour, you can,␀␀␀select any number of cards to discard before␀␀␀you fill up your hand again.-␀␀␀To discard a card, just drag and drop it into␀␀␀the Discard box.␀␀␀␀,␀␀␀This allows you to draw more cards and ditch)␀␀␀any unwanted ones. Don't worry, discarded+␀␀␀cards get shuffled back in your deck later.    	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀- End of Battle -␀␀␀␀.␀␀␀The battle is over! Regardless of win or loss,*␀␀␀what's important is that you start feeling$␀␀␀comfortable with the game mechanics.%␀␀␀Don't worry, keep at it until you do.'␀␀␀Remember that helpful tips and info can"␀␀␀always be found in the top screen.    ␀␀␀&␀␀␀In Campaign mode, every time you win a%␀␀␀battle you get a new pack of cards to␀␀␀increase your card collection. ␀␀␀Choose Manage Decks to put newly#␀␀␀acquired cards in your deck and use ␀␀␀them in upcoming battles. But...&␀␀␀Winning Campaign games is not the only␀␀␀way you can get new cards...␀␀␀␀)␀␀␀You can also get cards by playing against ␀␀␀your friends in Multi-Card Play.␀␀␀␀*␀␀␀So, what are you waiting for? Get together-␀␀␀with your friends, rack up the wins, and rake␀␀␀in the cards!    ␀␀␀)␀␀␀Keep in mind that these are just examples%␀␀␀of what cards can do! As you progress-␀␀␀through the game you'll discover that you can,␀␀␀create some incredibly powerful effects with!␀␀␀the right mix of cards and units.␀␀␀Now, select a card target!␀␀␀    ␀␀␀
