␀␀␀U   ␀␀␀%␀␀␀Sister! I am overjoyed! But - how did␀␀␀you ever find me here?N   ␀␀␀ ␀␀␀You do not remember the times we␀␀␀rested here after battle, then?U   ␀␀␀␀␀␀That was so long ago...N   ␀␀␀'␀␀␀I hope you will hark back to that time! ␀␀␀You once respected your sister's&␀␀␀wisdom... Please, stop this slaughter!U   ␀␀␀ ␀␀␀I will not! The Daevas have been#␀␀␀persecuted long enough. They see us#␀␀␀as demons, and we will act as such!N   ␀␀␀!␀␀␀We must put aside thoughts of war"␀␀␀or all sides will perish: Indians,␀␀␀Persians - and Daevas!U   ␀␀␀$␀␀␀So it is true! You did steal Aesma's␀␀␀troops!N   ␀␀␀ ␀␀␀Aesma's troops follow me because␀␀␀they yearn for peace!U   ␀␀␀#␀␀␀The only way Daevas will have peace'␀␀␀is if they are alone on this continent,␀␀␀sister of mine.N   ␀␀␀&␀␀␀You leave me no choice! I will not let'␀␀␀the bloodshed continue! Even if you are␀␀␀my brother!␀␀␀G   ␀␀␀"␀␀␀Sindra! I should have trusted you!N   ␀␀␀(␀␀␀It is hard to trust in these treacherous␀␀␀times... I understand.G   ␀␀␀␀␀␀We have suffered. Oh, and many␀␀␀others as well!N   ␀␀␀$␀␀␀My brother was broken by his ordeal.&␀␀␀I can see no way out but to fight him!G   ␀␀␀&␀␀␀I will apologize by finishing what you#␀␀␀have started. Today, this war ends.
